From: stockmind <slysimo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: clear the VP9 padding rows so 16-line alignment stops showing

Applies on top of 0430. Ours, not part of the LibreELEC series.

The capture buffer is sized to ALIGN(height, 16) because the engine writes the
reconstruct surface in 16-line blocks and the chroma plane has to sit where the
hardware puts it. Those padding rows are never reconstructed, so they keep
whatever the buffer held before, and consumers that size their surfaces from
G_FMT - Chromium's VA-API path - show them as a line of green/magenta noise at
the bottom of clips whose height is not a multiple of 16 (804, 234, 536...).
Reporting the coded height instead is not an option: it hangs the engine (see
0002's comment).

Clear the padding once per frame from cedrus_vp9_setup(), where the coded height
is known. ~23 KB at 1080p, nothing when the height is already 16-aligned.
Verified on the device with a 1920x804 VP9 file: decode stays bit-exact
(PSNR average:inf against software) and the bottom rows are black instead of
colour noise in Chromium.
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c
@@ -454,6 +454,35 @@
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * The capture buffer is 16-line aligned, so the last ALIGN(h,16) - h rows are
+ * padding: the engine does not reconstruct them and they keep whatever the
+ * buffer held from a previous frame.  Consumers that size their surfaces from
+ * G_FMT (Chromium's VA-API path) display those rows, which shows up as a line
+ * of colour noise at the bottom of clips whose height is not a multiple of 16.
+ * Clearing them costs ~23 KB per frame at 1080p and nothing when the height is
+ * already aligned.
+ */
+static void cedrus_vp9_clear_padding(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
+				     struct vb2_buffer *buf, u32 cur_h)
+{
+	struct v4l2_pix_format *fmt = &ctx->dst_fmt;
+	unsigned int pad = fmt->height - cur_h;
+	unsigned int bpl = fmt->bytesperline;
+	u8 *base;
+
+	if (!pad || fmt->height <= cur_h)
+		return;
+
+	base = vb2_plane_vaddr(buf, 0);
+	if (!base)
+		return;
+
+	memset(base + bpl * cur_h, 0, bpl * pad);
+	/* Interleaved chroma plane starts after luma; two lines per chroma line. */
+	memset(base + bpl * fmt->height + (bpl * cur_h) / 2, 0, (bpl * pad) / 2);
+}
+
 static void cedrus_vp9_ref_scale(u32 ref_w, u32 ref_h, u32 cur_w, u32 cur_h,
 				 u32 *reg0, u32 *reg1)
 {
@@ -1018,6 +1047,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Current frame reconstruction targets. */
+	cedrus_vp9_clear_padding(ctx, &run->dst->vb2_buf, cur_h);
 	luma = cedrus_dst_frame_addr(ctx, &run->dst->vb2_buf, 0);
 	chroma = cedrus_dst_frame_addr(ctx, &run->dst->vb2_buf, 1);
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VP9_CUR_LUMA_ADDR, VE_DEC_VP9_BUF_ADDR(luma));
